# tool_token_est.pdl - ESTIMATED token cost per work-intent route (2026-11-22; owner: "just use a common average from statistics, ratios are fine for now").
# EVERY number here is an ESTIMATE, not a measurement. Neither the model nor the harness can read real token use (tool_log rows say tokens=0 = not measured).
# Method: with_route = exec rows x call_tokens + read rows x avg_doc_tokens x section_fraction;
#   without_route = with_route + explore_extra_reads x avg_doc_tokens + explore_extra_calls x call_tokens   (the ASSUMPTION: without a route one wrong doc is read first and two extra search calls are made).
# MEASURED inputs: avg_doc_tokens = mean bytes/4 over 330 HQ-IQ-BOOK docs over 1 KB (depth 2), 2026-11-22; bytes_per_token 4 is the usual rule of thumb for English and code, off by up to about 30%.
# ASSUMED inputs: call_tokens, section_fraction, explore_extra_reads, explore_extra_calls. Each EST row follows the two formulas above from the RULE rows and the exec/read counts of its bank-work entry; only the RATIO is meant to be read.
# Biggest single item measured: harness/README.md is 162,017 bytes, about 40,500 tokens; a route must say "read the case header or grep one row", never "read the README".
RULE | bytes_per_token | 4
RULE | call_tokens | 600
RULE | avg_doc_tokens | 4005
RULE | section_fraction | 0.5
RULE | explore_extra_reads | 1
RULE | explore_extra_calls | 2
